This is my 2nd ascension. The main reason I'm bothering to post this is 
I just spent several hours teaching myself the workings of compiling and 
patching nethack to get a Dump-patched executable. Why isn't there just 
one out there for downloading? I'll bet a lot of folks play the 
unpatched version, and then when they finally ascend, the dump patch 
would be mighty handy.

Anyway, I got lucky on a lot of counts with this one. For starters, two 
altars on dlvl 1, two more before sokoban, and another five on the way 
to Medusa. Also started with a magic marker, yay.

Sacrificed at an altar on dLvl 3 extremely early on and got Magicbane 
almost immediately. That helps a lot.

I did Sokoban first and got the bag. I went back to the mines, but there 
was hardly anything noteworthy there. The lighting store had only 3 
candles (but one magic lamp, SDSM) and I never found more than 2 more so 
my last wish was for candles.

I found an awesome bones file around dLvl 12, including Eyes of the 
Overworld. They're awesome. Found another bones around dLvl 20 with 
highly enchanted corunathum, gaunts of dex, and speed boots to complete 
my AK.

After the quest I started polymorphing into a Xorn continuously (I got 
polycontrol from eating a ring). There are some HUGE advantages of 
running through rock, and the Eyes helped me find my way.

The rest of the dungeons were trivial. Magic mapping and detect treasure 
on each level found my way. As a Xorn, I didn't even have to go around 
anything. The castle wand was spent on magic markers and a PYEC (to play 
around with; I didn't really need any of the benefits), and the markers 
were used to genocide things on whims (like trolls and puddings, which 
normally are not worth it). I never used two of my magic markers at all, 
I don't think. The last wish was saved for candles, and a good thing too.

On the Astral Plane, I chose left first and met Famine, who I was 
completely unprepared for. Half my life gone in two hits! I had lots of 
"oLife Saving, and I just used 'em up instead of bothering to heal. The 
altar was the correct one, so I heard the choir...

